+ScanMatch
+---------
+
+.. autoclass:: lark.ScanMatch
+    :members:
+
+``Lark.scan(text, start=None)`` yields non-overlapping matches, choosing the
+longest valid prefix at the earliest matching offset. Each match has a
+``range`` of absolute start and end offsets and a ``value`` with the same
+structure or transformer result as ``parse()``. Empty matches are skipped;
+ignored terminals are excluded from the boundaries.
+
+Scanning supports LALR parsers with the basic or contextual lexer, without
+postlex. Inputs may be strings, bytes, or ``TextSlice`` objects. Slice matches
+and their line and column metadata retain positions in the original text.
+When multiple start rules are configured, ``start`` is required.
+
+Lexer callbacks may run on discarded candidates. A callback's ``ValueError``
+rejects that candidate; other exceptions propagate. Callback tokens must
+preserve source positions (use ``Token.update()`` when changing a token).
+
+
